cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or write about Sheet Sequencer, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Sheet Sequencer: Gmail outreach with automatic follow-ups from a Google Sheet"
abstract: >-
  Sheet Sequencer is a free, open-source Google Apps Script that sends personalized
  emails from a Google Sheet through your own Gmail account and automatically follows
  up in the same thread until the recipient replies. Send times are randomized within a
  weekday-morning window, the full schedule is visible and editable in the sheet, and
  replies, bounces and out-of-office messages are detected automatically. It runs on
  Google's servers with no third-party backend.
authors:
  - name: "Sheet Sequencer contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tmoula/gmail-followup-sequencer"
url: "https://github.com/tmoula/gmail-followup-sequencer"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-16"
keywords:
  - google-apps-script
  - gmail
  - google-sheets
